	You didn't have poison resistance.  One of the changes from v3.0j is
that when polymorphing large piles of items there is a possibility that some
items will be destroyed or a golem will be created (iron or clay, maybe stone
too).

>2) Is it a good idea to convert an altar of a priest like the one in the
>   gnome town? I know hw gets angry but it seems to me that he regularly has
>   a cursed scroll of create monster and forget it you are meat for the
>   rothes.

	I would wait to take on a temple priest until you're certain you could
kill him easily, or at the very least teleport out if it gets too hairy.  I've
had my clock cleaned once too often by angry priests to be too cavalier in my
dealings with them.

>3) What exactly does a spellbook of clairvoyance do for you?

	While the spell is in effect, it will periodically 'magic map' a small
region around you.

>4) I know blessed magic lamps always give wishes but if a potion has a djinni
>   in it can you be sure of getting a wish?

	If the potion has a djinn in it, you'll get a wish.  The problem is
determining whether or not the potion has a djinn in it.

>5) When I play a wizard I always get magicbane bestowed when offering.
>   However my brother has got 4 different things whilst playing his knight.
>   Is magicbane going to be the first thing I get or will it differ sometimes.

	Certain classes have certain weapons which they will _always_ be
awarded first.  Barbarians always get Cleaver, samurai always get Snickersnee,
valkyries always get Mjollnir, and wizards always get Magicbane.  Knights
probably should get Excalibur, but by the time they get a weapon from their
deity, they have probably already gotten Excalibur from another source.

